# A blueprint taken out of a value and applied: a plain function gives a blueprint inside
# an option, and the arm of a building `match` that takes it out builds it (Semantics
# ch. 4: a building `match`'s arm "is fixed for the life of the block and adds no path
# segment"; ch. 8: "a blueprint builds nothing until a block applies it", at the applying
# block's next positions; Type System ch. 2: a blueprint is an opaque handle and still a
# value). Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

?Pick: fn Bool, @a -> ?@a
fn ?Pick b, @w = if b: ? @w else: nil

@Pair: @unit
@Pair:
    Ui.Label($text=$"left")
    Ui.Label($text=$"right")

@Page: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Page b:
    match ?Pick b, @Pair:                                        # 0 and 1, or 0
        ? @t: @t
        nil: Ui.Label($text=$"none")
    Ui.Label($text=$"end")                                       # 2, or 1
